; The colors and fonts the examples share. Not a figure: each example imports what it uses.

; The colors are BRAIID's, RSM's design system, so a figure in mathterpiece's default style sits
; well in a default RSM document: paper is gray-0, ink is the body text (gray-900, gray-950 in
; dark), soft is gray-600, and the accents are shade 600 of BRAIID's red, green, yellow and
; blue. Each color has a dark value, which a page whose color-scheme is dark draws instead. BRAIID's
; dark mode mirrors its shades around 500, so an accent's dark value is the light value of its
; shade 400.
(color paper (light-dark '#ffffff' '#13181b'))
(color ink (light-dark '#3c4952' '#ced6dc'))
(color soft (light-dark '#8b9fad' '#7a8a99'))
(color red (light-dark '#db2728' '#f87172'))
(color green (light-dark '#158c7f' '#37cab6'))
(color yellow (light-dark '#e28800' '#ffd31b'))
(color blue (light-dark '#027ac7' '#38b4f8'))

; The fonts by what they are for. A page with BRAIID points each family at the document's
; (--mtp-house-variable-family: var(--font-body), and --font-mono for number and code), so a
; figure's text follows the typeface the reader picks.
(font variable (family '"Source Sans 3", sans-serif') (style 'italic') (size 18))
(font number (family '"Source Code Pro", monospace') (size 14))
(font code (family '"Source Code Pro", monospace') (size 13))
